  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "sTBfre+Xc2C9PAmRCmikvh9m84M=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:48:51.501Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The Academy page `04-Reference/06-Authorization/renown-sdk/00-Overview.md` opens its quick start with:\n\n```tsx\nimport { RenownUserProvider } from \"@renown/sdk\";\n```\n\nand describes `useUser`, session persistence and a `RenownAuthButton` as the SDK's React surface. Checked against the tree at v6.2.2-dev.74:\n\n- **`RenownUserProvider` appears nowhere** in `packages/**` or `apps/**`;\n- `@renown/sdk`'s root export list is `common`, `credential`, `crypto`, `discovery`, `init.browser`, `local-credential-verifier`, `profile`, **`renown-builder`**, `session` types, `switchboard`, `types`, `utils` \u2014 no React provider, and its subpaths are `./node`, `./crypto` and the three wallet adapters;\n- the React pieces live in **`@powerhousedao/reactor-browser`** (`useRenownAuth`, `RenownAuthButton`, `RenownProvider`), which is exactly what the SDK's own `COMPONENTS.md` says: \"React components and hooks for Renown authentication are provided by `@powerhousedao/reactor-browser`, not by `@renown/sdk` directly.\"\n\nSo the page describes an earlier, React-shaped SDK. A developer following it installs `@renown/sdk` and imports a symbol that does not exist. The authoritative pair is the SDK's `RenownBuilder` for construction and reactor-browser's `RenownProvider` / `useRenownAuth` for React \u2014 with `useUser` surviving only as a hook in `packages/reactor-browser/src/hooks/renown.ts`, not as an SDK export.\n\n## Provenance\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/06-Authorization/renown-sdk/00-Overview.md` \u2014 Quick Start \u203a 1. Wrap Your App with RenownUserProvider; Key Concepts (RenownUserProvider, useUser)\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:48:51.500Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:48:51.501Z"
    }
  },
